ring, N = 4: digits = ranks whose data a segment contains; start:
  rank 0:  seg0=0      seg1=0      seg2=0      seg3=0    
  rank 1:  seg0=1      seg1=1      seg2=1      seg3=1    
  rank 2:  seg0=2      seg1=2      seg2=2      seg3=2    
  rank 3:  seg0=3      seg1=3      seg2=3      seg3=3    
after reduce-scatter step 1 (add): 0->1:seg0 1->2:seg1 2->3:seg2 3->0:seg3
  rank 0:  seg0=0      seg1=0      seg2=0      seg3=03   
  rank 1:  seg0=01     seg1=1      seg2=1      seg3=1    
  rank 2:  seg0=2      seg1=12     seg2=2      seg3=2    
  rank 3:  seg0=3      seg1=3      seg2=23     seg3=3    
after reduce-scatter step 2 (add): 0->1:seg3 1->2:seg0 2->3:seg1 3->0:seg2
  rank 0:  seg0=0      seg1=0      seg2=023    seg3=03   
  rank 1:  seg0=01     seg1=1      seg2=1      seg3=013  
  rank 2:  seg0=012    seg1=12     seg2=2      seg3=2    
  rank 3:  seg0=3      seg1=123    seg2=23     seg3=3    
after reduce-scatter step 3 (add): 0->1:seg2 1->2:seg3 2->3:seg0 3->0:seg1
  rank 0:  seg0=0      seg1=0123   seg2=023    seg3=03   
  rank 1:  seg0=01     seg1=1      seg2=0123   seg3=013  
  rank 2:  seg0=012    seg1=12     seg2=2      seg3=0123 
  rank 3:  seg0=0123   seg1=123    seg2=23     seg3=3    
after all-gather step 1 (copy): 0->1:seg1 1->2:seg2 2->3:seg3 3->0:seg0
  rank 0:  seg0=0123   seg1=0123   seg2=023    seg3=03   
  rank 1:  seg0=01     seg1=0123   seg2=0123   seg3=013  
  rank 2:  seg0=012    seg1=12     seg2=0123   seg3=0123 
  rank 3:  seg0=0123   seg1=123    seg2=23     seg3=0123 
after all-gather step 2 (copy): 0->1:seg0 1->2:seg1 2->3:seg2 3->0:seg3
  rank 0:  seg0=0123   seg1=0123   seg2=023    seg3=0123 
  rank 1:  seg0=0123   seg1=0123   seg2=0123   seg3=013  
  rank 2:  seg0=012    seg1=0123   seg2=0123   seg3=0123 
  rank 3:  seg0=0123   seg1=123    seg2=0123   seg3=0123 
after all-gather step 3 (copy): 0->1:seg3 1->2:seg0 2->3:seg1 3->0:seg2
  rank 0:  seg0=0123   seg1=0123   seg2=0123   seg3=0123 
  rank 1:  seg0=0123   seg1=0123   seg2=0123   seg3=0123 
  rank 2:  seg0=0123   seg1=0123   seg2=0123   seg3=0123 
  rank 3:  seg0=0123   seg1=0123   seg2=0123   seg3=0123 

all-reduce of 240 elements per rank; 'sent' = elements sent by the busiest rank
   N  algorithm             rounds     sent sent/count  result
   2  ring                       2      240      1.000  correct
   2  recursive doubling         1      240      1.000  correct
   2  halving-doubling           2      240      1.000  correct
   2  binomial tree              2      240      1.000  correct
   3  ring                       4      320      1.333  correct
   3  recursive doubling         -        -          -  (needs a power of two)
   3  halving-doubling           -        -          -  (needs a power of two)
   3  binomial tree              4      480      2.000  correct
   4  ring                       6      360      1.500  correct
   4  recursive doubling         2      480      2.000  correct
   4  halving-doubling           4      360      1.500  correct
   4  binomial tree              4      480      2.000  correct
   8  ring                      14      420      1.750  correct
   8  recursive doubling         3      720      3.000  correct
   8  halving-doubling           6      420      1.750  correct
   8  binomial tree              6      720      3.000  correct
  16  ring                      30      450      1.875  correct
  16  recursive doubling         4      960      4.000  correct
  16  halving-doubling           8      450      1.875  correct
  16  binomial tree              8      960      4.000  correct
formulas: ring rounds 2(N-1), sent/count 2(N-1)/N; recursive doubling rounds log2 N, sent/count log2 N
